# Template only -- lists the variable names this stack's docker-compose.yml
# expects. Real values live in Infisical, never here and never in git.
# scripts/render-env.sh writes the actual .env next to this file on the host.
#

# --- Pangolin (newt) connection ---
# This stack runs `newt`, the client half of Pangolin -- the tunnel this
# homelab uses for externally-exposed services (as distinct from the
# separate Cloudflare Tunnel container in the Cloudflared stack; don't
# conflate the two, they're two different front doors). newt mounts the
# Docker socket directly (not through socket-proxy) so it can discover
# containers -- one of the known, not-yet-hardened Docker-socket exposures
# in this homelab.
#
# PANGOLIN_ENDPOINT: the URL of your Pangolin server this newt client
#   connects out to.
# NEWT_ID / NEWT_SECRET: the site/client credentials Pangolin issued for
#   this newt instance (generated when you register a new site in
#   Pangolin's dashboard).
PANGOLIN_ENDPOINT=REPLACE_ME
NEWT_ID=REPLACE_ME
NEWT_SECRET=REPLACE_ME
